.TH ECHO 1
.SH NAME
echo \- print words, or write them to a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B echo
.RI [ word ...]
.RB [ >
.I file
|
.B >>
.IR file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B echo
is a command built into the shell,
.BR sh (1).
It prints its words separated by single spaces, and a newline. After
.BI > " file"
the line replaces what
.I file
held (it is created, mode 0644, if it does not exist); after
.BI >> " file"
it is added at its end. The file name may also touch the
.B >
.RB ( >file ).
Words after the file name are ignored.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 if the file could not be written.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
echo first line > notes.txt
echo second line >> notes.txt
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cat (1),
.BR sh (1)
.SH BUGS
The only redirection in the shell: other commands always print to the
terminal.
